# Citation metadata, in the format GitHub and Zenodo both read.
#
# The same claim appears in three places: this file, the footer of the tool
# itself, and the manuscript's Availability section. Three copies of one string
# is three chances to disagree, so scripts/check-citation.mjs asserts this file
# against the constants in src/lib/site.ts, and the remaining diff against the
# manuscript is done by hand because nothing here can see that document.
#
# The DOI is deliberately absent. Zenodo mints it when the tagged release is
# archived, and a placeholder that looks like an identifier is worse than an
# absent one. Add it under `identifiers` once minted, and set CITATION_DOI in
# src/lib/site.ts at the same time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Antibody Titration Planner
abstract: >-
  A deterministic browser tool that plans an antibody titration series for flow
  cytometry. It reports the concentration at each point in every form the bench
  and the method record require, for a staining volume and a cell number the
  user must declare, and it records the basis of any vendor recommendation it
  was given. It determines what the series should be; it does not prepare it,
  analyse the resulting data, choose the optimal point, or determine whether any
  point saturates the target. No model, no imputation and no language model is
  applied to any reported value, and no data entered by a user leaves the
  browser.
authors:
  - family-names: Modi
    given-names: A.B.
    affiliation: Ligant AI Incorporated
# Matches APP_VERSION in src/lib/site.ts and the tag on the archived release.
# The leading v is kept so that this file, the footer and the tag are the same
# string rather than three conventions for one version.
version: v0.1.0
# To be set to the day the tag is cut, not the day this file was written. A
# citation whose release date precedes the released commit is wrong in the
# direction that matters: it points a reader at a tree that did not yet exist.
date-released: '2026-09-14'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/abmodi-ai/Ligant.ai-Antibody-Titration-Planner
url: https://benchtools.ligant.ai/antibody-titration-planner/
keywords:
  - flow cytometry
  - antibody titration
  - titration series
  - staining volume
  - cell therapy
  - reproducible research
